-- 22 validator runs, below `SchemaValid.shape_threshold` (25), so each keeps
-- its codec's validator worker, and each is written where it stands
-- (`schema.md` §6, *A validator run calls its worker where it stands*): its
-- own context, its worker called, and `Result.withDefault`'s answer beside
-- it. Each reads its record's `…Keep` and never its `…Drop`, so no worker
-- builds a `…Drop`: every record a worker returns has one field. Through one
-- shared runner every worker's record met every default in one variable,
-- which past 48 records (`Spec.zig`'s `max_sites`) escaped, and then every
-- worker built both fields.
import Json
import Node
import Schema exposing (Value)


type alias Alpha =
    alphaKeep : Int
    alphaDrop : Int


alpha : Value, Bool → Int
alpha v fresh =
    model : Alpha
    model =
        Result.withDefault
            (Json.decodeValue v)
            (if fresh then { alphaKeep = 0, alphaDrop = 0 } else { alphaKeep = 1, alphaDrop = 1 })
    model.alphaKeep


